    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d54">

                <pb facs="0068" n="54" xml:id="pg54"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710 Consultation (4)/11–1644: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-16T13:00:00-04:00">November 16,
                            1944—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:38 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1798. Department’s circular November 14, 7 p.m.<anchor n="42" xml:id="d54-f1"/>
                    Memorandum handed Foreign Minister November 14. He read it aloud and expressed
                    his personal satisfaction without [<hi rendition="#italic">with our?</hi>] point
                    of view but said he would discuss it with President and Vice President. He
                    emphatically expressed approval of plan that Argentina present its case at
                    conclusion of conference on postwar and peace matters and not at beginning.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d54-f1" n="42" xml:id="d54-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed. This circular authorized the presentation of the text contained in
                    the circular of November 12, for which see telegram 2006, November 12, 11 a.m.,
                    to Mexico City, <ref target="#pg43">p. 43</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
